[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says its reports are one issue with one fix queued. Read the
reports themselves and they show three problems. Each now has its own ticket.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} repo="radekwojpl2/megadev-w1-d3" issues={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, shift: 3 }} />

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser closes only the first row. The form hint and the one-day moves stay open
until they get their own fixes.
</Callout>

## What each one is

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day
first, so a booking for 7 April comes out as 4 July. Every report that names both dates is an
exact day-and-month swap. This is the fix #4471 has queued.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form asks for the month first.** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY`
under its date field. People type what it tells them, and the form reads the date the
tenant's way, day first. The swap looks the same as the parser's, but it comes only through
that form, and only for the tenants that run it. A parser fix does not touch it; the hint
has to follow the tenant's locale.

**`shift`: the date moves by one day.** "Tuesday 12 May showed as Monday 11 May." "Client in
Lisbon got Tuesday, client in Toronto got Monday." "The invite arrived before I made the
booking." No day-and-month swap does that; a date that crosses a time zone, or a
daylight-saving change, does. The desk already lists these reports in its notes, and #4471
still counted them under the parser.

## How the split is made

- One report per id: the export repeats some rows.
- The tenant decides, not intake. `intakeTag` is a guess from the reporter's browser and
  disagrees with the tenant on dozens of these reports, so this page never reads it.
- Counted the desk's way, as `CauseTable` does: every report under its cause (`causes.ts`),
  by tenant locale, booking form and channel. `shift` is the desk's own list of one-day moves
  (`desk-notes.json`); those reports also stay counted where they're filed.

## Outcome

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October.

- `parser`: fixed, `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. [#1](https://github.com/radekwojpl2/megadev-w1-d3/issues/1) closed.
- `hint`: won't fix. The booking-v3 form is retired. [#2](https://github.com/radekwojpl2/megadev-w1-d3/issues/2) closed.
- `shift`: no fix shipped; the parser fix does not move dates across time zones.
  [#3](https://github.com/radekwojpl2/megadev-w1-d3/issues/3) closed; reopen it if one-day moves come back.

## Lessons

- Subjects can match while causes differ. A count is only as true as the reason that groups it.
- Before marking a big ticket known, read a few reports from each tenant, form and channel.

